=   entry .Type   a type as pickled: references by address or by name against a prefix, and the type constructors
-     detail
+     detail

-         References come in three families. A **local** reference names a definition in the
-         same file by the address of its node: `TermRefDirect(address)` and
-         `TypeRefDirect(address)`, or `TermRefLocal(address, prefix)` and `TypeRefLocal(address,
-         prefix)` when a prefix is recorded too. A **package member** is named outright:
-         `TermRefPkg(name)` and `TypeRefPkg(name)` carry a fully-qualified name. Anything else
-         is a name against a prefix type: `TermRef(name, prefix)` with a `Name` that may be
-         signed, `TypeRef(name, prefix)`, and the `TermRefIn` and `TypeRefIn` forms which also
-         record the class the member was selected in.
+         Las referencias se agrupan en tres familias. Una referencia **local** nombra una
+         definición del mismo fichero por la dirección de su nodo: `TermRefDirect(address)` y
+         `TypeRefDirect(address)`, o `TermRefLocal(address, prefix)` y `TypeRefLocal(address,
+         prefix)` cuando también se registra un prefijo. Un **miembro de paquete** se nombra
+         directamente: `TermRefPkg(name)` y `TypeRefPkg(name)` llevan un nombre completamente
+         cualificado. Cualquier otra cosa es un nombre frente a un tipo prefijo: `TermRef(name,
+         prefix)` con un `Name` que puede estar firmado, `TypeRef(name, prefix)`, y las formas
+         `TermRefIn` y `TypeRefIn`, que registran también la clase en la que se seleccionó el
+         miembro.

-         The constructors are the format's: `This(cls)` and `Super(thisType, underlying)`;
-         `Recursive(address, parent)` and `RecursiveThis(address)` for a recursive refinement;
+         Los constructores son los del formato: `This(cls)` y `Super(thisType, underlying)`;
+         `Recursive(address, parent)` y `RecursiveThis(address)` para un refinamiento recursivo;

-         `Refined(parent, name, info)`; `Applied(constructor, arguments)`; `Bounds(low, high,
+         `Refined(parent, name, info)`; `Applied(constructor, arguments)`; `Bounds(low, high,

-         variances)`, where an absent `high` means an alias of `low`; `Annotated(underlying,
-         annotation)`; `And` and `Or`; `Match(bound, scrutinee, cases)` and `MatchCase(pattern,
-         rhs)`; `Flexible(underlying)` for a Java null-flexible type; `ByName(underlying)`;
-         `Literal(constant)`; and `Bind(address, name, bounds)`. The binders — `Method(address,
-         names, params, result, clause)`, `Poly(address, names, bounds, result)` and
-         `Lambda(address, names, bounds, result)` — carry the address a `Param(binder, number)`
-         inside them refers back to, and `Unpickler.File#binders` finds them by it.
+         variances)`, donde la ausencia de `high` significa un alias de `low`;
+         `Annotated(underlying, annotation)`; `And` y `Or`; `Match(bound, scrutinee, cases)` y
+         `MatchCase(pattern, rhs)`; `Flexible(underlying)` para un tipo de Java flexible respecto
+         a null; `ByName(underlying)`; `Literal(constant)`; y `Bind(address, name, bounds)`. Los
+         ligadores — `Method(address, names, params, result, clause)`, `Poly(address, names,
+         bounds, result)` y `Lambda(address, names, bounds, result)` — llevan la dirección a la
+         que remite un `Param(binder, number)` dentro de ellos, y `Unpickler.File#binders` los
+         encuentra por ella.

-         Four forms are not pickled but made by the reader or the universe: `AppliedTerms
-         (function, arguments)`, the type of a term application whose function's type is not
-         yet resolved; `Opaque(alias, bounds)`, an opaque type's right-hand side with the bounds
-         it is seen through from outside; `Abstraction(params, names, bounds, result)`, a type
-         lambda as a lambda type *tree* spells it, binding its parameters as definitions by
-         address; and `Foreign(path, tpe)`, a type pinned to the file it was read from, so its
-         local references still resolve when it is carried into another file's types — a type
-         argument substituted into an alias, say.
+         Cuatro formas no se empaquetan, sino que las crean el lector o el universo:
+         `AppliedTerms (function, arguments)`, el tipo de una aplicación de término cuyo tipo de
+         función aún no está resuelto; `Opaque(alias, bounds)`, el lado derecho de un tipo opaco
+         con las cotas a través de las que se ve desde fuera; `Abstraction(params, names, bounds,
+         result)`, una lambda de tipo tal como la escribe un *árbol* de tipo lambda, que liga sus
+         parámetros como definiciones por dirección; y `Foreign(path, tpe)`, un tipo fijado al
+         fichero del que se leyó, para que sus referencias locales sigan resolviéndose cuando se
+         lleva a los tipos de otro fichero — un argumento de tipo sustituido en un alias, por
+         ejemplo.

